   "id": "yevamot.59a.10",
   "daf": "59a",
   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "וְלֹא יִשָּׂא אֶת הַבּוֹגֶרֶת. תָּנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״וְהוּא אִשָּׁה בִבְתוּלֶיהָ יִקָּח״, פְּרָט לַבּוֹגֶרֶת — שֶׁכָּלוּ לָהּ בְּתוּלֶיהָ. דִּבְרֵי רַבִּי מֵאִיר. רַבִּי אֶלְעָזָר וְרַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן מַכְשִׁירִין בְּבוֹגֶרֶת.",
   "en": "§ It was taught in the mishna: «And» a High Priest «may not marry a grown woman. The Sages taught» that the verse: «“And he shall take a wife in her virginity”» (Leviticus 21:13) «excludes a grown woman, whose hymen has worn away,» i.e., it is no longer as complete as that of a minor or a young woman; this is «the statement of Rabbi Meir. Rabbi Elazar and Rabbi Shimon declare a grown woman fit» to marry a High Priest."
  }
 ],
